# GPU-fit tuning: Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q8_K_XL on 2x R9700 (MACHINE=r9700-dual).
#
# Sourced by run-vulkan.sh AFTER models/qwen3.8-27b-q8.env and BEFORE
# profiles/r9700-dual/default.env.
#
# The full-native-context option for this pair. Q8 weights cost 21 GiB less than
# BF16, which is exactly what buys the jump from 128K (see
# profiles/r9700-dual/qwen3.8-27b.env) to the model's native 262,144.
#
# KV math as in the BF16 profile: 16 of 65 blocks are full attention,
# 4 KV heads x head_dim 256 x (K+V) = 32,768 elements/token -> ~34 KiB/token
# at q8_0.
#
# Memory budget vs ~62 GiB combined VRAM:
#   weights (UD-Q8_K_XL)             29.3 GiB
#   KV @ 262,144 tok, q8_0 K+V        8.5 GiB
#   vision projector (mmproj F16)     0.9 GiB
#   compute buffers @ ubatch 512     ~1.5 GiB
#   ------------------------------------------
#   total                            ~40 GiB / ~62 GiB VRAM   (comfortable)
#
# The ~22 GiB of slack is real and usable: raise UBATCH to 1024 for faster
# prefill, or run PARALLEL=2 for two concurrent 131K slots (+8.5 GiB) if you are
# serving more than one client.
#
# NOTE: Q8 also fits a SINGLE R9700 (29.3 GiB weights on a ~31 GiB card), but
# only barely and with no room for a KV cache -- do not try it. Single-card use
# is what profiles/r9700/qwen3.8-27b-q4.env is for.
: "${CTX_SIZE:=262144}"
: "${UBATCH:=512}"

# --- split mode ----------------------------------------------------------
# Override the card default of `layer` (profiles/r9700-dual/default.env) for
# this DENSE model. Measured 2026-08-14, same prompt and settings both runs,
# 23-token prompt / ~155 decode tokens, thinking disabled:
#
#            prefill      decode
#   layer    74.23 t/s    15.75 t/s
#   row      98.56 t/s    17.24 t/s
#            +32.8%       +9.5%
#
# WHY: with `layer`, whole layers are assigned per card, so for a dense model
# card 1 idles while card 0 computes its half and vice versa -- rocm-smi showed
# the pair alternating (32/68, 65/41) and neither above ~68%. `row` splits each
# tensor across both cards so they compute concurrently.
#
# Decode gains little because single-stream decode is BANDWIDTH-bound, not
# scheduling-bound: each card reads half the weights but they read
# simultaneously, so wall-clock per token is unchanged. ~29.3 GiB of Q8 weights
# per token against ~640 GB/s puts the single-card ceiling near 21 t/s, and
# 17.24 is ~82% of that -- close to the practical limit for a dense 27B at
# 8-bit here. Prefill parallelizes over tokens, which is where row mode pays.
# The 23-token prompt understates that; real coding prompts should do better.
#
# Row mode also fixes a VRAM imbalance: under `layer` the KV cache and compute
# buffers land on card 0 on top of an even weight split, leaving GPU[0] at 97%
# allocated vs GPU[1] at 68% -- uncomfortably close to OOM.
#
# NOT applied to the Coder-Next profiles on purpose: that is an 80B MoE with
# ~3B active params, a very different traffic pattern, and row mode is untested
# there. Set SPLIT_MODE=layer inline to A/B this back.
: "${SPLIT_MODE:=row}"

# --- vision disabled on this host ----------------------------------------
# The model envs pass --mmproj (the model is natively VL). This host does not
# use it, and the projector costs ~0.86 GiB on the PRIMARY card -- which here
# is also the card driving the displays, and the one that runs out of VRAM
# first (it carries the KV cache and compute buffers on top of its weight
# share). --no-mmproj overrides the earlier --mmproj; verified against this
# image's llama-server, which loads text-only with both flags present.
#
# Machine-level, not model-level, ON PURPOSE: models/qwen3.8-27b*.env are
# shared with strixhalo, which has ~46 GiB spare and no reason to give up
# vision. Delete this line to re-enable images/video here.
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--no-mmproj)
